EXT. RAILROAD WATER TOWER PLATFORM - DAY

A prairie town reduced to a siding, a tank on stilts, and one plank platform baking in the sun. A dog sleeps in the shade of a barrel.

A WOMAN sits on a crate, shelling peas into a pan. ROSALIND "ROSIE" HARTWELL-BANDA (40s, calico dress, wide-brimmed hat). Calm. Too calm.

An old man whittles a spoon on the steps. ELIJAH TOBIAS CORNWALL (70s, white beard, suspenders).

A boy of twelve pumps the handle of the well. JEDEDIAH "JED" OKONJO (12, oversized boots).

A young cowhand leans against the post, hat low. He chews a straw. SANTIAGO "SANTI" PERALES-WINTERS (20s, spurs, easy grin).

At the far end, a rider. A stranger on a gray horse. He reins in. Climbs down slow.

His name is CORNELIUS DUNLEAVY-KEITA (50s, long coat, dusty). He nods to them all.

CORNELIUS
Afternoon.

ROSIE
Afternoon.

She keeps shelling. He ties the horse. Walks up the steps. Elijah scoots his boots out of the way.

CORNELIUS
Train due?

ELIJAH
Four o'clock.

CORNELIUS
That's a ways.

ELIJAH
Hot day for waiting.

Cornelius smiles. Takes off his hat and wipes his brow. Santi drops the straw. Picks up a new one.

CORNELIUS
That your boy at the pump?

ROSIE
He's everybody's boy.

Cornelius nods. Watches Jed work the handle. The water gushes into a trough.

JED
(to no one)
Mister, you want some?

CORNELIUS
I'd be obliged.

Jed fills a tin cup. Hands it up. Cornelius drinks. Slowly. Hands it back.

CORNELIUS (CONT'D)
Peas.

ROSIE
Peas.

CORNELIUS
I always liked them.

She finally looks up. Meets his eye.

ROSIE
Not these.

Cornelius lowers his hand. Santi straightens from the post. Elijah sets the knife on his knee. Jed backs away from the pump.

CORNELIUS
(quietly)
Ah.

Rosie reaches into the pan. Under the peas, a revolver. She lifts it, calm as a woman lifting a teacup.

ROSIE
Walk back to your horse.

He does not move.

ROSIE (CONT'D)
Now, Mr. Dunleavy.

He turns. Takes the steps one at a time. Reaches the gray. Swings up.

The dog lifts its head.

CORNELIUS
(to Rosie, over his shoulder)
Tell the boy to keep pumping.

He rides out.

Rosie sets the revolver back in the peas. Jed lets out a sob and sits right down in the dust.
